          "quote": "11.1 Upon expiry or termination for any reason, Vendor shall, at Customer's request, provide reasonable transition assistance for up to six months at the rates in the expiring Order Form. Assistance includes knowledge transfer, export support, cooperation with a replacement supplier, orderly migration, and continued service at the then-current scope and service levels.",
          "rationale": "Section 11 meets the preferred position on its material terms, so no redline is needed. § 11.1 applies \"[u]pon expiry or termination for any reason\" and gives us up to six months of transition assistance (knowledge transfer, export support, cooperation with a replacement supplier, migration, continued service at existing scope and service levels). § 11.2 requires return of all Customer Data within thirty days in a \"complete, commonly used, documented, machine-readable format\" with relationships and metadata, and expressly bars Vendor from withholding data over a fee dispute. § 11.3 requires secure deletion of remaining Customer Data after return, certified in writing by an authorized officer, with any law-required retained copy remaining protected and use-restricted. Two departures from the model wording both run in our favour and are noted only: (i) assistance is charged at the rates in the expiring Order Form rather than Vendor's then-current rates, which protects us from a post-termination uplift; and (ii) the thirty-day return clock runs from our request rather than automatically from termination, which leaves timing in our control and carries no data-loss risk because § 11.3 conditions deletion on our confirmation of successful return. Cross-references are consistent: § 16.5 confirms \"Customer Data remains governed by Sections 11 and 15,\" and § 10.1 preserves our rights in Customer Data after expiry or termination. No walk-away trigger (no data hostage, no immediate deletion) is present.",
